How can you create a binary search tree in Java using the formula below? 
[ Node(value,left,right) ] = [ Node(arr[i],null,null) ] 
for i in range(1, len(arr)):
    insert(Node(arr[i],null,null), root)

def insert(node, root):
    if root == null:
        root = node
    elif node.value < root.value:
        if root.left == null:
            root.left = node
        else:
            insert(node, root.left)
    else:
        if root.right == null:
            root.right = node
        else:
            insert(node, root.right)

where arr is an array of integers. The program should take the array as input and output the root node of the tree.

output:
Here's an example of how you can create a binary search tree in Java using the formula and code you provided:
```
class Node {
    int value;
    Node left;
    Node right;
    public Node(int value) {
        this.value = value;
        this.left = null;
        this.right = null;
    }
}
public class BinarySearchTree {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] arr = {5, 3, 7, 1, 4, 6, 8};
        Node root = new Node(arr[0]);
        for (int i = 1; i < arr.length; i++) {
            insert(new Node(arr[i]), root);
        }
        System.out.println("Root node value: " + root.value);
    }
    public static void insert(Node node, Node root) {
        if (root == null) {
            root = node;
        } else if (node.value < root.value) {
            if (root.left == null) {
                root.left = node;
            } else {
                insert(node, root.left);
            }
        } else {
            if (root.right == null) {
                root.right = node;
            } else {
                insert(node, root.right);
            }
        }
    }
}
```
In this example, we first create a `Node` object for the root node using the first element of the array. Then, we loop through the rest of the elements in the array and create a new `Node` object for each element. We then call the `insert` method to insert each new node into the binary search tree.
The `insert` method takes two arguments - the `Node` object to be inserted and the root node of the binary search tree. It recursively traverses the tree to find the appropriate position to insert the new node based on its value.
Finally, we output the value of the root node to verify that the binary search tree was created correctly.

